{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>et their hands and et their feet.</b> There was no need to say other than יְדֵיהֶם וְרַגְלֵיהֶם ('their hands and their feet'); rather, it intended to say that there is no washing for hands without feet and none for feet without hands. Therefore it said <b>et</b>, meaning together with their hands their feet, and together with their feet their hands. And these are the words of our Sages of blessed memory in Zevaḥim (Zevaḥim 19b), that one must sanctify hands and feet together."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:34:35.729425070Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}